    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1004",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Bagrichthys hypselopterus (Bleeker, 1852)</li><li><strong>Common name:</strong> Black Lancer Catfish</li><li><strong>Type locality:</strong> Palembang, Sumatra, Indonesia.</li><li><strong>Synonym:</strong> Bagrus hypselopterus</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> 400 mm or 15.7\" SL.</li><li><strong>IUCN Red List:</strong> Least Concern (last assessed 2018).</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1004",
      "html": "<p>Members of the highly specialized and unusually-shaped bagrid catfish genus Bagrichthys Bleeker, 1858, live in large muddy rivers throughout Southeast Asia and are characterised by their elongate and laterally compressed caudal peduncle, the dorsally-directed serrations on the posterior edge of the dorsal-fin spine, gill membranes united but free from the isthmus, and a long adipose fin without a free posterior margin (Roberts, 1989).</p><p>It is very unlikely this fish has ever been available to the aquarium hobby.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1004",
      "html": "<p>Asia: Thailand to Indonesia. Pacific, Greater Sunda Island Rivers, Borneo Waters; Pacific, Greater Sunda Island Rivers, Sumatra Waters.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1004",
      "html": "<p>pH: 6.0 - 7.0</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1004",
      "html": "<p>In the wild, the fish are detritivorous.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1004",
      "html": "<p>Males have an elongate genital papilla and longer barbels.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1004",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
